  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#45905\", \"PowerToys#33\", \"PowerToys#31721\"], \"answer\": \"This has been requested before: a way to choose which items appear in the compact (Windows 11) File Explorer context menu versus the full one. PowerToys#45905 is nearly identical, asking for a customiser like Office's ribbon editor. It was closed as a duplicate of PowerToys#33, the long-running umbrella request for managing and customizing the right-click menu, and PowerToys#31721 asked for an organizer to push items up or down between the first-level and 'Show more options' menus. The feature is not implemented in PowerToys, so there is no built-in setting to use today. Add your use case and a thumbs-up to PowerToys#33, which is where the team tracks this. In the meantime, the tickets mention third-party tools such as NilesoftShell, which can hide or remove existing menu entries. Note that items like 'Edit in Notepad' and 'Send to' come from Windows or other apps, not PowerToys.\"}",
